# direnv entry point: 'cd' into this directory and the devShell from
# flake.nix loads automatically (first time excepted -- run 'direnv allow').
#
# This only gets you the tools (west, cmake, ninja, ...), the same thing
# 'use flake' always gets you. It does not also turn the directory into a
# west workspace -- that bootstrap step lives in devshell.sh because direnv
# hooks are meant to be fast, and 'west update' is not. Run
# './devshell.sh west update' (or just './devshell.sh' for a shell) once
# after 'direnv allow', the same way a fresh clone needs one 'denver run' in
# ../zephyr-devshell-4.3.1.
use flake
